-b61e-4d9369b7037b', 'Logical Agents', 'logical agents', '# Logical Agents

## TL;DR / Quick Summary
*   **Logical Agents** are a type of **Intelligent Agent** that use **logic** to represent knowledge and make decisions [GFG], [TP].
*   They operate based on a **Knowledge Base (KB)** which stores facts and rules about the world [GFG], [TP].
*   **Propositional Logic** is a basic form of logic where knowledge is represented using simple true/false statements (propositions) [GFG], [TP].
*   Key components of a **Knowledge-Based Agent (KBA)** include **Perception**, **Knowledge Base**, **Inference Mechanism**, and **Learning** [GFG].
*   **Inference** is the reasoning process used to derive new conclusions from the KB, often using **Forward Chaining** or **Backward Chaining** [GFG].
*   **Axioms** are general truths about the environment, combined with **percept sentences**, to build the KB [GFG].
*   A major limitation of Propositional Logic-based agents is the **exponential computational cost** of inference over time [GFG].

## Introduction
In Artificial Intelligence, an **agent** is a system designed to perceive its environment, make decisions, and take actions to achieve specific goals, operating autonomously without direct human control [GFG]. Within this broad category, **Logical Agents** represent a sophisticated approach where decision-making is grounded in formal logic. These agents leverage a **Knowledge Base (KB)** filled with facts and rules about their world, employing logical reasoning to deduce appropriate actions [GFG].

This document focuses primarily on **Propositional Logic-based Agents**, which utilize **propositional logic** – a subset of mathematical logic dealing with statements that can be either true or false – to represent knowledge and make informed decisions [TP]. Such agents are fundamental to understanding how AI systems can reason and act based on explicit knowledge.

## Definition / Core Concept
A **Logical Agent** is an AI agent that uses formal logic to represent its knowledge about the world and to reason about its actions [GFG], [TP]. Its core functionality involves deducing what actions to take based on the information stored in its **Knowledge Base (KB)**, which combines general axioms about how the world works with specific percepts gathered from the environment [GFG].

A **Propositional Logic-based Agent** is a specific type of logical agent that employs **propositional logic** to express its understanding of the environment. It is a straightforward agent form that decides what to do based on logical statements [TP].

