  <img src="https://ik.imagekit.io/huwygg3fd/Gemini_Generated_Image_to7to5to7to5to7t.png" width="80%">
</p>

### 2. If There are Multiple Instances of Resources
When resource types can have multiple instances (e.g., several CPU cores, multiple disk drives), the situation is more complex [GFG].
*   **Detection**: In this case, the **presence of a cycle in the RAG is a necessary but not a sufficient condition for deadlock** [GFG]. A cycle may exist, but the system might not necessarily be in a deadlock if resources can be allocated from available instances to break the cycle.
*   For such systems, a more sophisticated **Deadlock Detection Algorithm** or the **Wait-For Graph Algorithm** is used [GFG].

