## Introduction
Embedded systems are specialized computational systems that integrate both hardware and software to perform a dedicated task [GFG]. They are found everywhere, from everyday home appliances to complex industrial machinery [GFG]. The heart of any embedded system is its software, which dictates its functionality and performance. Programming languages are the tools used to write this software, and their selection is critical, impacting factors like execution speed, memory usage, and direct hardware control [GFG]. This document explores the fundamental concepts of embedded systems and delves into key programming languages used for their development, with a specific focus on **Embedded C**.

